47:* ''A fifth face plane'', `@intents-<tag>`, beside `@persona`, `@circles`, `@identities` and `@sessions` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga">>). It derives from the PersonaGroup's tag like its siblings, so every device that joins the face derives its name and syncs it with no extra provisioning; two faces on one device share no entry; nothing stands above it. The PersonaGroup mints it and delegates append to each device edge; the mint order binds as for every face plane.
50:** `intent`: an invocation naming its verb, its arguments, its audience and its causal bound (#/no-clock). Its id is the content hash of issuer, verb, arguments and nonce, so every device derives it offline and a replayed copy carries the same id. An idempotent verb takes the empty nonce.
51:** `outcome`: a receipt whose `cause` names the intent's id and whose signer names the device that acted.
52:** `asks` and `answer`: an outcome that needs a hand (a human approval, a missing capability) names what answers it; any session wearing the face answers by an entry citing the ask's id.
54:** `supersede` and `cancel`: an issuer's or the operator's later word on an intent.
61:!! Who answers ~ stand-down first, idempotent effects as the floor, no election
66:# ''Safety lives in the effect.'' Every verb sorts into one of three classes, declared with the verb: ''idempotent or convergent'' (two answers harmless; keyed by the intent's id), ''per-device'' (its effect touches one vessel; one owner by construction), ''single-effect fleet-wide'' (two answers harm). The third class MUST NOT address "any device": an issuer pins its executor, or a human `answer` names the executing atom. An intent that breaks this refuses at issue.
67:# ''The winner reads, never elects.'' Where two outcomes stand for one slot after a merge, the outcome of the earliest device in the intent's own preference list counts; outside a list, the outcome whose `H(atom ‖ intent id)` reads lowest counts. Every other outcome stays in the log, marked a duplicate: the loser's act already happened, and its record stays visible.
74:!! No clock ~ nothing expires by time
77:* ''An intent voids by a causal event'' named in its bound: superseded by a later entry, its issuer's delegation revoked, the face's roster passing a named edge, or the operator's `cancel`. A device that merges the void before acting declines; one that acted before merging leaves a recorded act, never a silent loss.
78:* ''The operator's release always wins'': a `release` or `cancel` signed for the face outranks any claim, by authority, never by order.
79:* ''An `every` intent reaches a device that joins after it'', unless its bound names a roster edge; the reader evaluates the audience against the roster it holds.
80:* ''Compaction folds by the operator's act alone'': an answered intent and its outcomes fold into a summary entry when the operator runs the fold, never on a timer.
86:!! The far agent ~ an AI that acts from afar
88:An agent off every device of the face (a cloud sandbox, another machine) never holds an atom: a shared act never makes a shared secret.
90:* The agent holds its own key and a narrow delegation from the face: a verb prefix, an argument policy and a causal bound in place of an expiry time.
91:* It signs an `intent` and hands it to a ''relay seat'': a vessel of the face with a door off the local socket, opened per face, ring-gated and off by default. The relay verifies the chain and appends the entry carrying the AGENT's signature; it countersigns only its admission.
92:* The answering device signs the outcome with its atom, `cause` naming the invocation. A reader verifies agent → delegation → face, invocation → outcome, and atom → device edge → face, and trusts the relay for nothing after admission.
100:!! The rubric ~ what earns a place in a face's log
102:The operator's tension, 2026-10-20: //every little action must not end up in each face's log; each keystroke replaces a cached invariant tiddler in memory with another, so a draft mid-edit does not belong.// The plane carries a hand's ''decisions that cross devices'', never its ''motion''. An entry belongs on the plane only when every test below holds:
107:# ''It expects an answer.'' An intent addresses someone and awaits an outcome. A broadcast of state that nobody answers belongs on a plane or document of its own, never here.
110:''Granularity'': one entry per decision, never per change. A session's edits coalesce in working memory, and the hand's commit turns them into one intent at most. ''Progress'': no heartbeats; between an intent and its outcome only `claim`, `asks` and their answers appear; progress detail rests in the acting vessel's own bag. ''Rate'': the plane's entry rate follows the rate of decisions by humans and agents, never the rate of input; a witness counts entries per committed act.
115:| saving a tiddler in the face's own wiki | that wiki's bag and its own sync; no intent |
116:| "move this carrier to the crossroads" | an `intent`, its `outcome` on the plane |
117:| "admit this new device to the face" | an `intent` pinned to the hearth that holds the root |
118:| an agent's request for approval | an `asks`, answered by a session wearing the face |
128:!! The reds ~ what a test must show for the plane to hold
130:# Two partitioned devices both answer an idempotent intent addressed to a class; after the merge the effect equals one run, one outcome counts and both stand recorded.
132:# A pinned intent never runs on another device, though that device holds the capability.
135:# A replayed intent keeps its id and draws no second effect; the control, a fresh nonce, draws a new id.
136:# An `every` intent draws one outcome per device, never one in all (dedupe stays scoped to the audience slot).
137:# Two faces on one vessel share no entry; a device that joins a face derives the plane and syncs it with no provisioning.
138:# A far agent's intent, admitted by a relay, verifies on a device that never saw the relay; a revoked delegation refuses on read, the revocation arriving first or after; a relay that alters an argument breaks the signature.
139:# A device asleep across a voiding event declines on waking; an intent with no bound gets honored.
141:# The rubric holds: a hundred keystrokes and one save in a face's wiki write no entry; one "move to crossroads" writes one intent and one outcome. A seeded duplicate-answer fixture trips the duplicate counter before a zero gets trusted.
147:!! The build ~ roadmap row `I1`
149:Row `I1` at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> carries the build, red-first in this order: the plane and its entry kinds; stand-down and the verb classes; the read-side winner; claims, takeover and causal voids; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane (closing "two hearths of one face"); the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness; then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. The CLI's per-invocation face naming (the session model's commit 5) lands beside the summons move, since an intent names its issuing face.

