59:!! The hands ~ every hand opens a session, and hands differ by profile, never by key
79:* ''A standing grant names the face a seat wears.'' The grant rests at the MCP mount. The owner verifies it afresh at every open, and it opens nothing while the vessel rests at the floor: no spirit works on a locked vessel.
80:* ''The Mask travels as authorship.'' A write into a shared realm carries the hand that made it as a field of the record, beside the face that signs: the kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask. The field names and authorizes nothing; no gate reads it. A Mask pins to no key and no identifier, so it counts as no pet-name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy">>).
81:* ''An agent's dissent drafts; a person's ask edits'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). An agent that disagrees with a person's edit files its own version as a draft beside it, and the person's edit stands until the person chooses: an agent never overrides. A person who asks an agent to edit a tiddler directly makes that edit the person's own act (the ''attended'' position above), and the agent writes it, reaching only the tiddlers the ask names and only under the asker's own write authority.
82:* ''A projected wiki stands as a surface.'' One tree on disk serves the person. A wiki names a face's relation to a composition (#/the-working-layer), so each face's wiki takes its own folder and the path says whose wiki it holds. No file and no `.meta` chooses the signer: an edit returns under the face of the session that leases the surface. A switch advances the generation, and an edit sensed under an earlier generation surfaces as a draft.
83:* ''Files that changed while no session held the lease'' ingest at the next mount, under the mounting face, as surfaced drafts.
87:* ''One verb table serves every hand.'' A seat sees every verb, and a verb beyond its profile refuses by name.
88:* ''A seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority'' (an attended spirit acts as the operator, so this bound falls on a standing one alone): a vault or custody verb, an admit, a kapae, a quorum signature, a face switch, or a residency move into a bag. A seat MAY draft such an act for a person to sign.
89:* ''Authority only narrows down a chain of spirits.'' A spirit MAY seat a sub-spirit under a profile no wider than its own, and the Mask records the chain.
90:* ''A container makes the profile bind.'' A spirit that shares its operator's OS account reaches every door that operator reaches, and its declared hand stays a declaration. A spirit that runs in a container holding only its seat's socket and grant holds no other door.
98:!! The working layer ~ one document per face relation, wiki, and slot kind
202:* ''A per-terminal hint MAY soften the naming.'' The vessel re-verifies the hint on every use, and the hint grants nothing.
203:* ''`persona wear` switches the caller's LIVE session.'' An interactive CLI keeps that face until it exits.
204:* ''Attribution derives from the verified face.'' A caller's own `requestedBy` reads as display text alone.
222:* ''The shared worker spawns no child worker.'' The holder, the Repo, the lock, the route table and the daemon kernel all run in its own runtime. A tab-created worker launches the wiki engine; the page mints no grant and hands that worker no unrestricted sync port.
223:* ''Nobody opens a second Repo.'' When the holder dies, every volatile session dies with it. Tabs wait for the lock to release, open a new owner, and ask for fresh sessions. No tab trusts an earlier greeting.
224:* ''Where a browser offers no shared worker'', one tab MAY hold the lock as the single owner and further tabs refuse by name.
246:* ''A CLI run'': the socket closes or the process exits; an explicit close; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
247:* ''A tab'': the page's close signal; a lost port; the holder's death; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
248:* ''An abrupt tab loss'' may send no close. The holder reclaims an unresponsive lease by a ''local monotonic liveness budget''. That budget frees resources and never judges a relation: it expires no face, no admit and no grant (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/no-global-now">>).
249:* ''An observed revocation'' closes the sessions that depend on the revoked relation and records the causal fence. A replica holding no later history answers //as of the last verified fence// or //incomplete//. It invents no current standing and no lapse by a wall clock; an act that needs a fresher relation refuses by name.
259:# ''Freeze and preflight.'' New calls on this session freeze. The owner preflights the target face's custody or delegation, admit, causal relation, absolute planes, proof subject and effective recipes, as immutable descriptions. It MUST NOT mount the target face before the old facets fall: one session would then hold two live face views. A refused preflight leaves the old generation live.
260:# ''Write the intent.'' A vessel-private switch intent gets written and flushed: the causal position, the outgoing face and the incoming face.
261:# ''Fence the old generation.'' Its dials stop, its operation and signer facets fall, its scoped document channels close, and its surfaces and islands dispose. An effect in flight resolves through its durable receipt.
262:# ''Advance, mount, dial.'' The generation advances. The target surfaces mount under the new scoped view, and the session dials with fresh keys under the target face's proof.
263:# ''Write the outcome.'' A mount or a dial that fails at commit closes this session and reports the partial outcome; the caller opens afresh. Nothing restores the old face's authority in silence.
275:* ''One vessel-wide selector.'' `wearPersona` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-vault.ts`) moves one active pointer; the node and browser openers (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`, `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`) each resolve one worn face at vessel boot.
276:* ''A broad sync port, on every production mount.'' Every wiki island mounts through the pool's wiki door (`mountWiki`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts`) and boots a Repo over a transferred `syncPort`, which carries unrestricted Repo sync.
277:* ''A wiki door keyed by wiki alone.'' That door keys its slots by `wikiId`, so two tabs of one wiki fold into one island.
278:* ''A holder that answers the asker and fences its epoch, faceless.'' The shared holder delivers each island message by one closed route table (`packages/lararium-browser/src/holder-routes.ts`): a reply to the port that asked, camera traffic to the port that leases the camera, the island's own asks to the port whose manifest it took; it drops the rest by name and broadcasts nothing. It mints one random `ownerEpoch` per boot and one random `sessionId` per port, greets each port with its envelope, and refuses by name, to that port alone, a message with no envelope, another owner's epoch, an unknown session, another port's session or another generation; the island sees no envelope (`packages/lararium-browser/src/shared-holder-core.ts`, the tab's half in `shared-holder.ts`). These sessions carry the maintenance channel and wear no face.
279:* ''A CLI over the local socket'' with caller-generated request ids and durable outcomes (`packages/lares-cli/src/local-connector.ts`, `packages/lararium-node/src/uds-channel.ts`); no socket binds a session to a face.
280:* ''A watcher that names its own destination.'' `lares watch --source <dir> --to <bagUri>` takes the bag from its caller and submits each wave under the vessel's identity (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`); no lease and no face stands between a disk edit and its signature.
284:* ''The hands' profiles.'' `face`, `verb`, `ingest` and `seat` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-contract.ts`). A session carries one from its open to its end, and a switch of face keeps it.
285:* ''The scoped document view'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`). It answers announcements, fetches, writes, catalog names and content reads from the session's own facets.
286:* ''The one recipe resolver'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/surface-recipe.ts`). It returns absolute ids and a revision at surface mount.
287:* ''The pool's surface door'' (`mountSurface`). It keys an island by the whole session key, opens the view over exactly what the recipe resolved, and hands the island no store, no catalog, no disk mirror and none of the vessel's own doors. A surface island's events take a door of their own and never the one that places vessel verbs. `closeSession` ends a session in good order and `fenceSession` closes its views first; from either, the session mounts nothing again.
288:* ''The face a session wears, and its signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, over `face-authority.ts` and `face-proof-subjects.ts`). One function joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the PersonaGroup's private grant into the `face` value, and derives the proof subject and the four planes itself; a signer mints for one live session, asks the owner's table before every signature, and drops at a close or a switch.
289:* ''The island's half'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts`, `view-channel.ts`). An island whose manifest carries a view stands under the minted peer id, lays the resolved slots, asks its view for catalog names and content, runs no recipe watch, and settles its writes before it acks a teardown.
293:# ''The contract in mesh.'' The session type, its validators, the port and socket binding, and refusal of a stale owner epoch or generation.
294:# ''Scoped document access.'' The session-scoped view over announcements, fetches, writes, catalog and content-addressed reads; no durable per-island store. The view, the pool's surface door and the island's half stand specified in code. The debt closes when every interactive surface mounts through that door, which waits on a verified face (debt three) and on callers that hold a session (debts five and seven). Four hunks close with it: the share verdict's caller reads the pool's view for an island's peer, the leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon, the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves, and a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask.
295:# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody rows for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed">>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus; a face at two Nexuses waits on this contract's word.
296:# ''The recipe resolver and the pool's identity.'' The working-layer binding follows #/the-working-layer; two same-face sessions take two islands, a repeated exact mount opens one, and a recipe write reaches the next mount by sync without changing a live mount. The resolver and the whole-key pool stand specified in code, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. The working-layer binding stays owed and waits on the join door, where the face secret arrives. The callers stay owed too: the compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount, the browser's plugin selection folds into it, and the wiki door, its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller.
297:# ''Node callers move to sessions.'' Two CLI sessions wear different faces at once over one Repo; a copied socket and a cross-face receipt read both refuse; a same-face receipt reads after the CLI that asked has exited.
298:# ''The browser holder as owner.'' Two tabs show one backing Repo and one held lock; a failed daemon boot refuses both, releases the lock and permits a retry. The routing and the faceless envelope stand (#/standing-and-owed). The face-bearing `session:open`, `session:call` and `session:switch` wait on the face supplier's browser caller, `W4` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops">>), and the holder's custody fork waits on the operator.
299:# ''Browser surfaces.'' Two tabs mount one wiki under separate sessions; frames and control answers reach their source surface alone; no wiki engine runs on the page's main thread.
300:# ''The switch, and the selector retires.'' Switching one session leaves another live; an old generation's effect never paints the new face; no boot path reads a vessel-wide active face.
301:# ''The disk as a surface.'' The watcher opens a session and leases each projected wiki; a disk edit returns under the leasing session's face; an edit from an earlier generation and a file changed under no lease both surface as drafts; a move between two faces' folders asks for a copy by name.
302:# ''The seat.'' An MCP connection opens a session under a standing grant, verified at each open and refused at the floor; its profile writes the working layer alone.
303:# ''The Mask as authorship.'' A record written into a shared realm carries its kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask, as a field no gate reads; a session cannot write another hand's mark.
304:# ''Door parity at the session.'' A CLI run and an MCP connection open the same session kinds and draw the same named refusals; a seat's refused verb names its profile; a seat drafts an authority act and cannot sign one; a sub-spirit's profile never exceeds its parent's.

